<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0703">Corollary <span data-tag="0703">9.7.1.22</span> <span class="named">(Relative Cocompletion as an Adjoint)</span>.</a> Let $\mathbb {K}_0 \subseteq \mathbb {K}$ be collections of simplicial sets and let $\lambda $ be an uncountable regular cardinal. Assume that there exists a regular cardinal $\kappa &lt; \lambda $ such that $\lambda $ has exponential cofinality $\geq \kappa $ and each $K \in \mathbb {K}$ is essentially $\kappa $-small. Then the inclusion functor </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}^{ \mathbb {K}-\mathrm{cocont}}_{&lt; \lambda } \hookrightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}^{ \mathbb {K}_0-\mathrm{cocont}}_{&lt; \lambda } \]
</div>
<p> admits a left adjoint, given by the formation of $\mathbb {K}$-cocompletion relative to $\mathbb {K}_0$. </p>
</article>
